  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "A right triangle \\(ABC\\) with hypotenuse \\(AB\\) has side \\(AC=15.\\) Altitude \\(CH\\) divides \\(AB\\) into segments \\(AH\\) and \\(HB,\\) with \\(HB=16.\\) The area of \\(\\triangle ABC\\) is",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(120\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(144\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(150\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(216\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(144\\sqrt5\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": "150"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1984-p17.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(AH=h.\\) Similarity in the right triangle gives \\[ \\begin{aligned} AC^2&=AH\\cdot AB,\\\\ 225&=h(h+16), \\end{aligned} \\] so \\(h=9.\\) Hence \\(AB=25.\\) Also \\(CH=\\sqrt{AH\\cdot HB},\\) so \\(CH=\\sqrt{9\\cdot16}=12.\\) The area is \\(\\frac12\\cdot25\\cdot12=150.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Use the right-triangle projection relation \\(AC^2=AH\\cdot AB\\)",
        "After finding \\(AH,\\) use \\(CH^2=AH\\cdot HB\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
